<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1975" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">almus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		alo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>nourishing</i>, <i>affording nourishment</i>,
				<i>cherishing</i> (<b>poet.</b>
			epithet of Ceres, Venus, and other patron deities of the earth, of
			light, day, wine, etc.; cf. Bentl. ad <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				4, 13</span></i>).—Hence, <i>genial</i>, <i>restoring</i>, <i>reviving</i>, <i>kind</i>, <i>propitious</i>, <i>indulgent</i>, <i>bountiful</i>,
			etc.: O Fides alma, Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Off.
				3, 29, 104</span></i> (Trag. v. 410 Vahl.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nutrix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 2, 3, 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Venus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr. 1,
					2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4, 15, 31</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mater terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 992</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 231
			al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ceres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. G.
					1, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoebe,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					A. 10, 215</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cybele,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10, 220</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. G.
					2, 330</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vites,</span>”
				<i>refreshing</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 233</span></i>
			 al.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Faustitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 5, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Maia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 2, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Musae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 4, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 7, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sol,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. C. S.
					9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adorea, i.e. gloria, quae virtutem nutrit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					C. 4, 4, 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pales,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 722</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacerdos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					5, 9, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ubera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. Achill. 2, 383 al.</span></i>
			</div>
